# Shotgun source of truth

Follow `AGENTS.md`, `docs/product.md`, and `docs/architecture.md`. If a task needs a new dependency, table, secret, or product decision, record it in `docs/decisions.md`.

Do not invent schema, payments, chat, admin, or extra tables from older prompt packs. Those are not the spec.

## Do

- Implement only the assigned issue (or the smallest demo slice if there is no issue).
- Inspect existing code and tests before adding abstractions.
- Keep screens free of direct maps, routing, identity, gas-price, and notification API calls — one typed module per concern.
- Treat remaining seats as server-derived; clients must not freely write seat availability.
- Enable and respect RLS on every exposed table.

## Don't

- Add Stripe or any in-app payment processing.
- Put service-role keys or other secrets in the Expo bundle or Git.
- Add Redux or a second component library unless the assigned issue requires it.
- Duplicate or override `AGENTS.md` with a parallel product model.
